      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town of Porum was named for John Porum Davis, a rancher, Civil War veteran, and Cherokee Nation councilman.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porum%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Porum formed in 1905 when two smaller communities, Porum Gap and Starvilla, merged into one town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porum%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Midland Valley Railroad arrived in the Porum area in 1903, bringing new settlement and speculation to the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porum%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Between 1906 and 1916, Porum was the site of the Porum Range War, a conflict between the Davis, Starr, and Hester families.",
